We operate under a hybrid grant model that includes:
Open applications (Open Grant Pool);
• Individual grant programs from partners (Grant Programs);
• Thematic and regional initiatives.
• Grants can range from local projects to international initiatives depending on the donor.

Who can apply:
• Non-profit organizations;
• Charitable foundations;
• Social enterprises;
• Initiative groups;
• Individual participants (depending on the program).
Note: Each program has its own criteria specified in the description.

At this stage of the platform's development, DoGood does not fund grants with its own funds. We act as a platform that:
• Connects grantmakers and projects;
• Ensures transparency of the process;
• Simplifies the selection process and interaction.
Funding is provided directly by partners or grantmakers.

No. DoGood does not guarantee funding, but significantly increases the chances of projects through:
• High visibility of the project to donors;
• Direct access to the grantmakers' database;
• Structured and professional application submission.

Selection is carried out by grantmakers based on:
• Social impact (Impact);
• Relevance to the program theme;
• Quality of implementation and team;
• Budget transparency.
In the future, an AI recommendation system will also be implemented on the platform to improve matching.

We recommend:
• Clearly describe the problem the project solves;
• Show real and measurable impact;
• Provide a detailed and transparent budget;
• Avoid vague and general wording.

You can:
• Write via the feedback form on the website;
• Contact us by email: startup@dogood.ink
